@@ -99,6 +99,7 @@ Usage: ./uniaxial-polycrystal --help
 | `--macroscopic-secant-acceleration`, `--no-macroscopic-secant-acceleration` | bool | `false` | Update the lateral compliance of the fixed point on `Sxx` and `Syy` by Broyden's secant method instead of using the elastic one at each iteration (fewer resolutions of the mechanical problem once plasticity develops). |
 | `--enable-post-processing`, `--disable-post-processing` | bool   | `true`           | Execute or not the post-processing steps.                                                                                                     |
 | `--enable-paraview-export`, `--disable-paraview-export` | bool   | `true`           | With the post-processing steps, export or not the displacement to ParaView at each step; the averages of the stresses per grain (file `avgStressPolycrystal`) are always computed. |
+| `--single-material`, `--material-per-grain` | bool | `false` | One material for all the grains, whose orientations are given point by point, instead of one material per grain: the behaviour is integrated by one batch over all the grains (on a GPU, one kernel per phase instead of one per grain). The averages of the stresses per grain are written in the same file `avgStressPolycrystal`. |
 | `--enable-export-von-Mises-stress`, `--disable-export-von-Mises-stress` | bool   | `false` | Export or not the von Mises stress.                                                                                               |
 | `--enable-export-first_eigen_stress`, `--disable-export-first_eigen_stress` | bool   | `false` | Export or not the first eigen stress.                                                                                         |
 
@@ -174,6 +175,8 @@ This table shows the comparison between the simulated Cauchy stress values and t
 
 `ctest` runs `UniaxialPolycrystalTest` (one time step of 0.2 s without post-processing, whose axial stress `Szz` is compared to the one computed by Cast3M, `results/polycrystal_cast3m.csv`, with a relative tolerance of 1 %, by `cmake/run-and-check.py`, which requires Python 3; without it, the case is only run), `UniaxialPolycrystalTest-DisplacementGradient` (the same with `--displacement-gradient`), `UniaxialPolycrystalTestPar` (the same on 2 processes) and `PolycrystalTestWithPostProPar` (one time step of 0.01 s on 2 processes, exporting the von Mises stress and the first eigen stress). With the option `MM_OPERA_HPC_GPU_TESTS` (see the main README), `UniaxialPolycrystalTest-gpu` and `UniaxialPolycrystalTest-mixed-gpu` run the first test with `--execution gpu` and with `--execution mixed --behaviours-execution cpu`.
 
+With the option `--single-material`, `UniaxialPolycrystalTest-SingleMaterial` compares the same axial stress to the one of Cast3M. `UniaxialPolycrystalTest-SingleMaterial-Comparison` and `UniaxialPolycrystalTestPar-SingleMaterial-Comparison` (on 2 processes) run two time steps of 0.2 s with and without the option, each run in its own directory, and compare the main output files and the averages of the stresses per grain (`avgStressPolycrystal`) of the two runs (`cmake/run-and-compare.py`): relative tolerances of 1e-9 on the main output file and of 2e-5 on the averages, written with 6 digits (1 % in single precision).
+
 ## References
 
 [^1]: JOSIEN, Marc. Mérope: A microstructure generator for simulation of heterogeneous materials. Journal of Computational Science, 2024, vol. 81, p. 102359.
